ne Rafinesque, a nineteenth-century polymath genius who concocted a dense, fantastical prehistory of the New World. Back in modern times, Sullivan takes us to the Ozarks for a Christian rock festival; to Florida to meet the alumni and straggling refugees of MTV's Real World, who've generated their own self-perpetuating economy of minor celebrity; and all across the South on the trail of the blues. He takes us to Indiana to investigate the formative years of Michael Jackson and Axl Rose and then to the Gulf Coast in the wake of Katrina--and back again as its residents confront the BP oil spill. Gradually, a unifying narrative emerges, a story about this country that we've never heard told this way.","publicationYear":2011,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"LITERARY COLLECTIONS / Essays","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-pulphead-essays-john-jeremiah-sullivan"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"SOCIAL SCIENCE / Popular Culture","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-pulphead-essays-john-jeremiah-sullivan"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"SOCIAL SCIENCE / Essays","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-pulphead-essays-john-jeremiah-sullivan"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Social life and customs","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-pulphead-essays-john-jeremiah-sullivan"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Popular culture","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-pulphead-essays-john-jeremiah-sullivan"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Essays (single author)","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-pulphead-essays-john-jeremiah-sullivan"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"New York Times reviewed","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-pulphead-essays-john-jeremiah-sullivan"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"ope